The inclusion of 26Ω series resistors in the outputs serves several purposes. Firstly, it helps to reduce the risk of damage from overcurrent conditions by limiting the current that can flow through the output pins. Secondly, it can help to reduce electromagnetic interference (EMI) by dampening the sharp edges of the output signals, which can be a source of noise in digital systems. Lastly, the resistors can also help to improve the signal integrity by reducing reflections on the transmission lines, which can be particularly important in high-speed digital systems.

\boxed{The 3.6V tolerant inputs and outputs allow for compatibility with a wider range of voltage levels, while the 26Ω series resistors in the outputs help to protect against overcurrent, reduce EMI, and improve signal integrity.}

